<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Exam 3 Review Session: the slides of the in-class review, with their
  worked solutions.

  The deck is the instructor's own HTML file (math14-exam3-review-slides,
  Nov 2026), unchanged, at assets/exam3-review-slides.html; it is served
  from the external directory and embedded here in an iframe, the way
  subsec-brain-map.ptx embeds the brain map, with a link to open it full
  size.  Six problems (substitution and the Jacobian, mass and center of
  mass, Green's theorem, flux through a surface, Stokes' theorem, and
  reasoning without computing), each followed by its solution slides.
  The solutions are posted, so the full deck is the same in every book.

  The "sec-exercises-" id prefix lets assets/unnumbered-chapter.css hide
  its number like the rest of the chapter.  Included at the end of the
  assignments chapter of the skeletal book (MATH14-Skeletal), the
  skeletal instructor book and the completed instructor book; the three
  copies are identical.
-->
<section xml:id="sec-exercises-exam3-review-session" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Exam 3 Review Session</title>

  <p>
    The slides of the Exam 3 review session, with worked solutions. Six
    problems: substitution and the Jacobian, mass and center of mass,
    Green's theorem, flux through a surface, Stokes' theorem, and a
    question to answer without computing. Sections:
    <xref ref="section-mass-center-of-mass" text="title"/>,
    <xref ref="section-jacobian-substitution" text="title"/>,
    <xref ref="section-surface-integrals" text="title"/>,
    <xref ref="section-greens-theorem" text="title"/>, and
    <xref ref="section-stokes-theorem" text="title"/>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Try each problem before you look at its solution. In the slides,
    <q>Next</q> (or the right arrow key) reveals a solution one step at a
    time, and <q>Read all</q> shows every slide on one scrolling page.
    For comfortable reading,
    <url href="external/exam3-review-slides.html" visual="">open the slides full size in a new tab</url>.
  </p>

  <interactive xml:id="interactive-exam3-review-slides" iframe="exam3-review-slides.html" width="100%" aspect="4:3">
    <instructions>
      <p>
        One problem per slide, followed by its solution. <q>Next</q> and
        <q>Back</q> move through the slides and the steps of a solution;
        <q>Read all</q> stacks every slide on one page.
      </p>
    </instructions>
    <static>
      <p>Slides of the Exam 3 review session (view in the HTML version).</p>
    </static>
  </interactive>

</section>
